WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.009
Here's how to open Terminal on a Mac and start Claude Code in your Documents folder.

2
00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:09.888
First, press ⌘ Command + Space to open Spotlight search.

3
00:00:10.888 --> 00:00:13.013
Type “Terminal”, then press Return.

4
00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:19.098
Terminal opens in your home folder (~). The word before the % shows the folder you're in.

5
00:00:20.098 --> 00:00:27.261
Type cd ~/Documents and press Return. cd means “change directory”.

6
00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:33.346
To check where you are, type pwd and press Return. You're in Documents.

7
00:00:34.346 --> 00:00:40.249
Now type claude and press Return. Claude Code starts and can work with the files in this folder.

8
00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:48.356
That's it: ⌘ Space → Terminal → cd ~/Documents → claude. You'll need Claude Code installed first.
